sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-raup-audit-raup-shell-coiling-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Raup shell coiling morphospace — Morphometric validation: 45/100" ;
        rdfs:comment "Shape quantities are now measured on the rendered geometry - W, D and T recovered from each mesh, height/width and spire/width per panel - written to a CSV, printed, shown on the still, and re-derived independently in the measurements sidecar; recovered values equal the inputs to 5e-15 in the script's own check and, in the sidecar's independent derivation, exactly for W and T and to 3e-4 for D (the aperture's inner margin is read off a 100-point grid). That is validation of the implementation against the definitions, and it is complete. What the dimension also asks for - a comparison with specimens or with the paper's own figures - is absent: no published W, D, T of a real shell, and none of Raup's block-diagram placements, is compared with anything here. Evidence: create_raup_animations.py L110–L131: recover_parameters(): W, D, T, height/width, spire/width from the mesh <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/create_raup_animations.py#L110-L131>; create_raup_animations.py L189–L204: write_metrics(): the CSV <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/create_raup_animations.py#L189-L204>; raup_shell_metrics.csv (generated output, not in repo): six rows, nominal and recovered values — raup_shell_metrics.csv: rendered output of create_raup_animations.py at ba6fd20, text/csv, 483 B, sha256 384d298d81f5373f754f790c2fa6560b93f8cf9164028a160b4df80810680057. Measurements (measure_outputs.py): recovered translation rate T, 'Planispiral' (W=3.0, D=0.0, T=0.0) = 0.0 ratio (reference 0.0, Raup's definition of T (dz_c/dr_c), Noshita 2014 / Okabe & Yoshimura 2017; should equal the input) [Δz_c / Δr_c of the generating-curve centre over the last revolution of raup_shell()] — height/width = 0.629, spire/width = 0.000; recovered distance from axis D, 'Planispiral' (W=3.0, D=0.0, T=0.0) = 0.0003 ratio (reference 0.0, Raup's definition of D; should equal the input) [inner margin / outer margin of the aperture (min/max radial distance of the last generating curve)]; recovered whorl expansion W, 'Planispiral' (W=3.0, D=0.0, T=0.0) = 3.0 ratio (reference 3.0, Raup's definition of W; should equal the input) [centre distance from the axis at the aperture / one revolution earlier]; recovered translation rate T, 'Turreted' (W=1.3, D=0.05, T=3.5) = 3.5 ratio (reference 3.5, Raup's definition of T (dz_c/dr_c), Noshita 2014 / Okabe & Yoshimura 2017; should equal the input) [Δz_c / Δr_c of the generating-curve centre over the last revolution of raup_shell()] — height/width = 1.142, spire/width = 0.858; recovered distance from axis D, 'Turreted' (W=1.3, D=0.05, T=3.5) = 0.0502 ratio (reference 0.05, Raup's definition of D; should equal the input) [inner margin / outer margin of the aperture (min/max radial distance of the last generating curve)]; recovered whorl expansion W, 'Turreted' (W=1.3, D=0.05, T=3.5) = 1.3 ratio (reference 1.3, Raup's definition of W; should equal the input) [centre distance from the axis at the aperture / one revolution earlier]; recovered translation rate T, 'Evolute disc' (W=2.0, D=0.45, T=0.0) = 0.0 ratio (reference 0.0, Raup's definition of T (dz_c/dr_c), Noshita 2014 / Okabe & Yoshimura 2017; should equal the input) [Δz_c / Δr_c of the generating-curve centre over the last revolution of raup_shell()] — height/width = 0.321, spire/width = 0.000; recovered distance from axis D, 'Evolute disc' (W=2.0, D=0.45, T=0.0) = 0.4501 ratio (reference 0.45, Raup's definition of D; should equal the input) [inner margin / outer margin of the aperture (min/max radial distance of the last generating curve)]; recovered whorl expansion W, 'Evolute disc' (W=2.0, D=0.45, T=0.0) = 2.0 ratio (reference 2.0, Raup's definition of W; should equal the input) [centre distance from the axis at the aperture / one revolution earlier]; recovered translation rate T, 'Conical' (W=3.5, D=0.0, T=1.5) = 1.5 ratio (reference 1.5, Raup's definition of T (dz_c/dr_c), Noshita 2014 / Okabe & Yoshimura 2017; should equal the input) [Δz_c / Δr_c of the generating-curve centre over the last revolution of raup_shell()] — height/width = 0.805, spire/width = 0.481; recovered distance from axis D, 'Conical' (W=3.5, D=0.0, T=1.5) = 0.0003 ratio (reference 0.0, Raup's definition of D; should equal the input) [inner margin / outer margin of the aperture (min/max radial distance of the last generating curve)]; recovered whorl expansion W, 'Conical' (W=3.5, D=0.0, T=1.5) = 3.5 ratio (reference 3.5, Raup's definition of W; should equal the input) [centre distance from the axis at the aperture / one revolution earlier]; recovered translation rate T, 'High-spired' (W=1.6, D=0.1, T=2.5) = 2.5 ratio (reference 2.5, Raup's definition of T (dz_c/dr_c), Noshita 2014 / Okabe & Yoshimura 2017; should equal the input) [Δz_c / Δr_c of the generating-curve centre over the last revolution of raup_shell()] — height/width = 0.998, spire/width = 0.738; recovered distance from axis D, 'High-spired' (W=1.6, D=0.1, T=2.5) = 0.1002 ratio (reference 0.1, Raup's definition of D; should equal the input) [inner margin / outer margin of the aperture (min/max radial distance of the last generating curve)]; recovered whorl expansion W, 'High-spired' (W=1.6, D=0.1, T=2.5) = 1.6 ratio (reference 1.6, Raup's definition of W; should equal the input) [centre distance from the axis at the aperture / one revolution earlier]; recovered translation rate T, 'Globose' (W=3.0, D=0.1, T=1.0) = 1.0 ratio (reference 1.0, Raup's definition of T (dz_c/dr_c), Noshita 2014 / Okabe & Yoshimura 2017; should equal the input) [Δz_c / Δr_c of the generating-curve centre over the last revolution of raup_shell()] — height/width = 0.628, spire/width = 0.341; recovered distance from axis D, 'Globose' (W=3.0, D=0.1, T=1.0) = 0.1002 ratio (reference 0.1, Raup's definition of D; should equal the input) [inner margin / outer margin of the aperture (min/max radial distance of the last generating curve)]; recovered whorl expansion W, 'Globose' (W=3.0, D=0.1, T=1.0) = 3.0 ratio (reference 3.0, Raup's definition of W; should equal the input) [centre distance from the axis at the aperture / one revolution earlier]." ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-raup-shell-coiling-morphometric-validation> ;
        pk:hasProbability "0.45"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-raup-shell-coiling-morphometric-validation> rdfs:label "Raup shell coiling morphospace (create_raup_animations.py, 1966-raup.py) satisfies the MorphoEval 0.1.0 criterion 'Morphometric validation' for Coiled molluscs in general; the six panels are labelled cf. Nautilus, Turritella, an ammonite, Conus, Cerithium, Helix (resemblance, not specimens)" ;
        dct:identifier "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (Cursor agent)" .
}

